{
  "id": "praeteritum-sein-haben",
  "name": "Past of be: was and were",
  "level": "A1",
  "status": "entwurf",
  "subtitle": "Use was and were to talk about the past: I was at home. They were in Leeds. Was goes with I, he, she and it. Were goes with you, we and they. Time words such as yesterday, last week and two years ago help.",
  "briefMarks": ["was", "were", "yesterday", "last week", "two years ago"],
  "source": "EnglishAcademy original English text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-10-29)",
